{
  "abstract": "We report transverse momentum ($p_{T} \\leq15$ GeV/$c$) spectra of $\\pi^{\\pm}$, $K^{\\pm}$, $p$, $\\bar{p}$, $K_{S}^{0}$, and $\\rho^{0}$ at mid-rapidity in p+p and Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{_{NN}}}$ = 200 GeV. Perturbative QCD calculations are consistent with $\\pi^{\\pm}$ spectra in p+p collisions but do not reproduce $K$ and $p(\\bar{p})$ spectra. The observed decreasing antiparticle-to-particle ratios with increasing $p_T$ provide experimental evidence for varying quark and gluon jet contributions to high-$p_T$ hadron yields. The relative hadron abundances in Au+Au at $p_{T}{}^{>}_{\\sim}8$ GeV/$c$ are measured to be similar to the p+p results, despite the expected Casimir effect for parton energy loss.",
