      "title": "Figure3.7: Double ratio vs $p_T$ in 0-12% Au+Au collisions.",
      "uuid": "4a8ab81b-b065-428f-b2fb-f6dd7d3afdbc"
    }
  ],
  "data_abstract": "BNL-RHIC. We report transverse momentum ($p_T \\leq 15$ GeV/c) spectra of $\\pi^{\\pm}$, $K^{\\pm}$ and $p$, $\\bar{p}$, $K^0_S$, and $\\rho^0$ at mid-rapidity in p+p and Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}} = 200$ GeV. Perturbative QCD calculations are consistent with $\\pi^{\\pm}$ spectra in p+p collisions but do not reproduce $K$ and $p$($\\bar{p}$) spectra. The observed decreasing antiparticle-to-particle ratios with increasing $p_T$ provide experimental evidence for varying quark and gluon jet contributions to high-$p_T$ hadron yields. The relative hadron abundances in Au+Au at $p_T > 8$ GeV/c are measured to be similar to the p+p results, despite the expected Casimir effect for parton energy loss.",
  "data_keywords": {
    "cmenergies": [
      {
        "gte": 200.0,
        "lte": 200.0
      }
    ],
